---
description: RTL logical properties and the accessibility floor
globs: **/*.tsx,**/*.jsx,**/*.css,**/*.scss
alwaysApply: false
---

Arabic is a first-class direction, not a later port. Physical box properties are
`no-restricted-syntax` errors.

| Never | Always |
| --- | --- |
| `marginLeft` / `marginRight` | `marginInlineStart` / `marginInlineEnd` |
| `paddingLeft` / `paddingRight` | `paddingInlineStart` / `paddingInlineEnd` |
| `borderLeft` / `borderRight` | `borderInlineStart` / `borderInlineEnd` |
| `left` / `right` | `insetInlineStart` / `insetInlineEnd` |
| `textAlign: "left" \| "right"` | `textAlign: "start" \| "end"` |
| `flexDirection: "row-reverse"` | let `dir` drive the flow |

Directional icons mirror automatically under `dir="rtl"` — pass
`mirror={false}` only for a glyph that must not flip.

Accessibility (`jsx-a11y` at `strict`, all errors):

- Never a `<div onClick>`. Use `Button`, `IconButton` or `Link`.
- `IconButton` requires `label`. `Icon` is `aria-hidden` unless given `label`.
- Every field has an associated label — `FormField` wires the ids.
- No `autoFocus`. No `tabIndex` on non-interactive elements.
- Focus-visible paints a 2px ring at 2px offset. Never remove it.
- Overlays trap focus, close on Escape, restore focus to their trigger.
- A field's error message replaces its hint — never render both.
